<!--
<h2>FriendLists - section [<i>friend_list_N</i>]</h2>

A FriendList is represented by the #LinphoneFriendList object. It is a list of #LinphoneFriend (contacts) that is stored locally on the device, and may be captured or synchronized with a remote server.
There are currently different types of friendlist:
- Pure local friend list, stored in local sqlite3 database
- friend list stored locally, but initally fetched from an HTTP server such as VCARD file, and re-captured at each Core or application start up
- friend list stored locally, but synchronized in both directions with a CardDAV server. With this type of friend list, each change to the list and its contacts (#LinphoneFriend) performed by the local user is pushed on the server, and any change present on the server is pulled by the client. This typically allows synchronisation of contact lists between several client devices, or may simply be to pull down a contact list from a server, and get it refreshed from the server in a more efficient way than the VCARD file method.

Table \ref friendlist_parameters "friendlist parameters" lists all parameters one may find under section [<i>friend_list_N</i>] of a Linphone RC file.<br/>
<table>
	<caption id="friendlist_parameters">Friendlist parameters</caption>
	<tr><th>Key<th>Value type<th>Possible values<th>Default value<th>Description</th></tr>
	<tr><td rowspan="3">type</td><td rowspan="3">string</td><td>local</td><td rowspan="3">local</td><td rowspan="3">The type of friendlist, i.e. the way it is expected to work</td></tr>
	<tr><td>carddav</td></tr>
	<tr><td>vcard</td></tr>
	<tr><td>uri</td><td>string</td><td>any file or HTTP/HTTPS URI</td><td>""</td><td>The URI from which the friendlist is synchronized to (Applicable only to carddav or vcard friendlist types)</td></tr>
	<tr><td>name</td><td>string</td><td>any UTF-8 string</td><td>""</td><td>A display name for this friendlist</td></tr>
</table>
-->

<h2>Authentication - section [<i>auth_info_N</i>]</h2>

The auth_info sections provide authentication information to use for SIP as well as http services (typically remote provisioning, cardDav requests). They need to be supplied in the form of a #LinphoneAuthInfo object, whose configuration storage representation is of [<i>auth_info_N</i>] sections, numbered continuously from 0.<br/>
Table \ref authinfo_parameters "authentication information parameters" lists all parameters one may find under section [<i>auth_info_N</i>] of a Linphone RC file.<br/>
<table>
	<caption id="authinfo_parameters">Authentication information parameters</caption>
	<tr><th>Key<th>Value type<th>Possible values<th>Default value<th>API</th>
	\if DOXYFILE_USE_COPYBRIEF
		<th>Description</th>
	\endif
	</tr>
	<tr><td>username</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_username()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_username</td></tr>
	<tr><td>domain</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_domain()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_domain</td></tr>
	<tr><td>passwd</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_password()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_password</td></tr>
	<tr><td>realm</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_realm()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_realm</td></tr>
	<tr><td>ha1</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_ha1()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_ha1</td></tr>
	<tr><td>algorithm</td><td>string</td><td>MD5</td><td>MD5</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_algorithm()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_algorithm</td></tr>
	<tr><td>authorization_server</td><td>string</td><td>any HTTP/HTTPS URI</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_authorization_server()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_authorization_server</td></tr>
	<tr><td>token_endpoint</td><td>string</td><td>any HTTP/HTTPS URI</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_token_endpoint_uri()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_token_endpoint_uri</td></tr>
	<tr><td>client_id</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_client_id()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_client_id</td></tr>
	<tr><td>client_secret</td><td>string</td><td>anything</td><td>""</td><td>linphone_auth_info_set_client_secret()</td><td>\copybrief linphone_auth_info_set_client_secret</td></tr>
</table>

